      "content_summary": "Guidance on handling security alerts such as audit log gaps, unexpected access denials, and privilege escalations within the OAuth Service and Permission Engine.",
      "content_body": "When users report missing audit entries or unexpected logouts, first verify if credential rotation was completed without propagating to all dependent services. Improper access reviews often lead to lingering elevated privileges or account lockouts that appear as policy violations. Check for known product limitations regarding certificate warnings which may trigger false positives in security scans. If the issue persists, perform a manual permission update to resync the Permission Engine state with the directory. For issues stemming from unpropagated rotations, a forced credential rotation cycle typically resolves the discrepancy."
