      "content_summary": "Troubleshooting misconfigured integrations, conflicting settings, and failed configuration propagation in Config Manager that lead to service unresponsiveness or feature flag failures.",
      "content_body": "If Config Manager shows config drift or feature flags failing to apply, first check for conflicting configuration settings that may have been introduced during an integration update. Customer configuration errors or operator mistakes often result in missing environment variables, causing the service to become unresponsive. Validate the policy definitions to ensure no syntax errors are preventing propagation. In legacy workflows, resolving these issues required manual documentation corrections and extensive customer education on proper variable precedence. Now, ensure the configuration change is committed and trigger a sync to clear the drift."
