      "content_summary": "Resolving timeouts, HTTP 504 errors, and connection resets in Webhook Engine caused by firewall rules, DNS failures, or proxy misconfigurations.",
      "content_body": "When Webhook Engine requests fail with timeouts or HTTP 504 errors, investigate potential firewall rules blocking outbound traffic or incorrect DNS configurations preventing host resolution. Packet loss or connection resets often stem from misconfigured proxies or load balancers not properly handling long-lived connections. Check certificate warnings which may indicate expired or invalid SSL chains interrupting secure handshakes. Apply firewall rule updates to allow necessary ports and correct DNS settings to ensure reliable delivery. If the issue persists, reconfigure the load balancer to handle webhook traffic more efficiently."
